{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/General Term of an Arithmetic Progression.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/General Term of an Arithmetic Progression.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"general term of an arithmetic progression general term of an arithmetic progression","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/General Term of an Arithmetic Progression.md","fileName":"General Term of an Arithmetic Progression.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"General Term of an Arithmetic Progression","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:41\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Sequences and Algebraic Patterns]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Sequences and Algebraic Patterns","Common Difference","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/General Term of an Arithmetic Progression.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/General Term of an Arithmetic Progression.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"general term of an arithmetic progression general term of an arithmetic progression","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/General Term of an Arithmetic Progression.md","fileName":"General Term of an Arithmetic Progression.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"General Term of an Arithmetic Progression","heading":"General Term of an Arithmetic Progression","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The general term of an arithmetic progression gives its value at position (n) without listing earlier terms. If the first term is (a_1) and the [[Common Difference]] is (d), then\n\n$$a_n=a_1+d(n-1).$$\n\nThe factor (n-1) appears because no difference has yet been added at the first position. For (2,7,12,17,\\ldots), the formula is (2+5(n-1)). Setting this expression equal to a proposed value tests whether that value occurs at a natural-number position.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Sequences and Algebraic Patterns","Common Difference","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/General Term of an Arithmetic Progression.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/General Term of an Arithmetic Progression.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"general term of an arithmetic progression general term of an arithmetic progression","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/General Term of an Arithmetic Progression.md","fileName":"General Term of an Arithmetic Progression.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"General Term of an Arithmetic Progression","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[algebraessentials.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Sequences and Algebraic Patterns","Common Difference","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}